{
  "dom_id": "step-q107105",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3,$ and its subset $B=\\{a{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in Q\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\nIV. $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t$ are two polynomials from $B,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t)+({a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{3}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}){t}^{2}+({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $B$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},\\,{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}$ are in $Q.$ So, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(t)={t}^{2}$ and $k=\\sqrt{2},$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B,$ because $\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"",
